healthy, and the error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 says v2.3.1 failed health checks, explains the rollback and the recovery, and lists next steps. Those are finding the root cause before redeploying, and checking how v2.3.1 reached production after its release candidate also failed in staging. My first attempt to create the incident timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops a duplicate from being created. The list now shows only INC-0001.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P3umXDchfMaJq9PKu4X46p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FiL1tU3vXrBZvSQGcEL6qC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RYK4PwiPU63zzRn7soZQ4u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Jtc4ai6ES6yJQvyXE6WX8z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RX3L5GvkxNpmtuLMi924kF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017umJGWcJAKDcFBBxoWNa2H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest 